C(212,[415],[244,246,248,250,289,291,293],'D283-285,353-374,472-505,609-652; E354-400,427-470,508-517','q ⊣ i ⊣ tau ⊣ rho; Proposition1.','For a nonnegative graded ring S and finite cutoffs N<=Nprime, q is quotient by the submodule generated below Nprime, i inclusion, tau high truncation, and rho(Q)_a=Hom_S^a(S_{>=Nprime-a},Q), a>=N. The counit tau rho→id is an isomorphism.','proved/sketched; later organized as Proposition1','E','These are restriction/extension adjunctions for the small preadditive category of degrees. Kelly1982 §§4.13–4.15 gives exact Kan-extension formalism; Stacks015Z verifies the injective consequence. The result is elementary categorical background, not a later de Rham theorem.','Correct finite-cutoff formulas, with arrow/index alarms listed separately. Finite localization does not settle C216–C219.',['late_Kelly1982','late_Stacks015Z'],['L04'],proof='proofs.md §3 independent verification of all four adjunctions and counit.')
